examples: {10: 60, 11: 10, 12: 24, 19: 18, 20: 60, 50: 300, 5: 20, 2: 3, 3: 8, 4: 6, 25: 100, 250: 1500}
max pi(n)/n for n <= 20000: 6.0; attained at [10, 50, 250, 1250, 6250]
split pi | p-1 and inert pi | 2(p+1), primes 7..NMAX: exceptions []
primes < 400 with maximal period: split pi = p-1: [11, 19, 31, 41, 59, 61, 71, 79, 109, 131, 149, 179, 191, 239, 241, 251, 269, 271, 311, 359, 379, 389] ; inert pi = 2(p+1): [7, 13, 17, 23, 37, 43, 53, 67, 73, 83, 97, 103, 127, 137, 157, 163, 167, 173, 193, 197, 223, 227, 257, 277, 283, 293, 313, 317, 337, 367, 373, 383, 397]
Q^k mod 5 scalar for k = [5, 10, 15, 20] ; Q^5 mod 5 = ((3, 0), (0, 3)) ; det Q = -1 = 4 = 2^2 is a square mod 5, so Q lies in PSL(2,5) = A5
